\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
Must every stable C2 solution $v:R^7\to [-1,1]$ of Delta $v=v^3-v$ be identically +1 or $-1$, or have the planar form $tanh((a\cdot x-b)/\operatorname{sqrt}(2))$ for a unit vector a and real b, without an energy-growth or asymptotic end-state assumption?

\subsection{Short English statement}
Must every stable C2 solution $v:R^7\to [-1,1]$ of Delta $v=v^3-v$ be identically +1 or $-1$, or have the planar form $tanh((a\cdot x-b)/\operatorname{sqrt}(2))$ for a unit vector a and real b, without an energy-growth or asymptotic end-state assumption?

